# Generated by Ask CK PyTest Creator for AWPTCM-T33247 — (19) IPv4_ARP - Clear ARP
# Standardized ART framework script. Frame is fixed; test logic is filled per step.
#
# ==== OBJECTIVE — expected results this script must demonstrate ====
#   - Dynamic ARP entries removed from the ARP cache on a clear-all request, with static
#   entries retained.
#   - A single dynamic entry removed when cleared by its IP address, all other cache entries
#   left intact.
#   - Cleared entries relearned through normal ARP resolution once traffic to the neighbour
#   resumes, with forwarding restored.
#   - A clear within a VRF removing only that VRF's dynamic entries, leaving entries in the
#   global table and other VRFs unchanged.
#   - A clear for an address with no matching entry, or for a non-existent VRF, rejected or
#   ignored with no change to the cache.
#   - The ARP cache shown empty of dynamic entries for the cleared scope immediately after
#   the clear.
